<title>USA: Harte-Hanks to explore divestiture.</title>
<headline>Harte-Hanks to explore divestiture.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harte-Hanks Communications Inc said Wednesday it planned to explore the divestiture of its daily newspapers, associated publications and television station.  </p>
<p>The company said it had retained Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Securities Corp as financial advisor.</p>
<p>It said it was thinking about divesting from six dailies, about 25 associated non-daily publications and sole television station, KENS-TV, the affiliate in San Antonio of Westinghouse Electric.</p>
<p>The company said it would prefer to divest its newspaper operations to a single acquirer. KENS-TV could be included in the newspaper transaction or transferred separately to another acquirer, it added.</p>
